  "summary": "This paper treats the chain ladder method as a supervised learning task by embedding actuarial judgement into hyperparameters of a convex loss function, enabling data-driven calibration while preserving interpretability and governance. It demonstrates practical application on real Schedule P data with clear workflow for incurred and paid reserving stages."
